# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Accessibility Standards (Guide #1)

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-ACCESSIBILITY-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

All customer-facing UI **MUST** meet **WCAG 2.2 Level AA**. Read the full guide before shipping any UI change.

## Non-negotiables

- Correct **semantic HTML** and ARIA only where native semantics are insufficient.
- **Keyboard operable** — no mouse-only critical paths.
- **Visible focus** indicators; logical focus order.
- **Color is never the sole information carrier** — pair with text/icon/pattern.
- Images/icons have appropriate **alt text** or `aria-hidden` when decorative.
- Form fields have **programmatic labels**; errors linked to fields.
- Modals/drawers: focus trap, escape to close, return focus on dismiss.
- Tables: correct headers/scope; not layout tables for data.
- Motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Touch targets meet minimum size guidelines in the full doc.

## Verification

Re-read the guide's completion checklist before marking UI work done.
